      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1780828887437,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Encapsulation in Java is an object-oriented principle that binds\ndata and methods into a single unit, typically a class.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Encapsulation in Java is an object-oriented principle that binds data and methods into a single unit, typically a class.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "sd1owTYzgoaf4lgshOAPs",
